00:17:29,160 --> 00:17:33,117
wow that was close i was
starting to think i'd just

248
00:17:33,200 --> 00:17:35,337
have to crawl out from there
like a cockroach and hope

249
00:17:35,420 --> 00:17:38,197
for the best that power of
yours is really handy in

250
00:17:38,280 --> 00:17:41,997
a pinch huh even so i'm
afraid that this is as far as

251
00:17:42,080 --> 00:17:44,617
i'll be able to accompany
you they're quite insistent

252
00:17:44,700 --> 00:17:47,877
on placing me in those c
prism stone handcuffs and once

253
00:17:47,960 --> 00:17:51,537
they take my cloak you'll
have nowhere to hide i just

254
00:17:51,620 --> 00:17:54,877
wish i wish i could do more
to help you but oh don't

255
00:17:54,960 --> 00:17:57,597
talk like that you got me
in this place didn't you

256
00:17:57,680 --> 00:18:00,157
that's more than i could
have done alone even though

257
00:18:00,240 --> 00:18:02,257
there's guards everywhere
we made it all this way no

258
00:18:02,340 --> 00:18:04,237
problem i can handle the rest

259
00:18:04,320 --> 00:18:10,377
luffy breaking your brother

260
00:18:10,460 --> 00:18:12,937
out will be challenging
enough but if you get captured

261
00:18:13,020 --> 00:18:16,417
as well who knows what
horrors you might face one

262
00:18:16,500 --> 00:18:18,657
wrong step and you may
never see the light of day

263
00:18:18,740 --> 00:18:24,600
again i know you want to save
ace but this is dangerous

264
00:18:25,380 --> 00:18:27,580
Please take care of yourself, too.

265
00:18:29,640 --> 00:18:30,960
I won't let you down.

266
00:18:31,080 --> 00:18:32,017
You have my word.

267
00:18:32,100 --> 00:18:33,417
Thanks for everything, Hancock.

268
00:18:33,500 --> 00:18:34,441
You're the best.

269
00:18:35,260 --> 00:18:38,900
I won't forget what you've done,
not for the rest of my life.

270
00:18:39,760 --> 00:18:41,620
He just called me by my name.

271
00:18:42,220 --> 00:18:44,540
My real, actual name.

272
00:18:44,800 --> 00:18:46,200
For the first time.

273
00:18:47,680 --> 00:18:48,510
Cool.

274
00:18:48,593 --> 00:18:50,257
Whatever works for you, Hammock.

275
00:18:50,340 --> 00:18:52,337
Can I get snap control over here, Hammock?

276
00:18:52,420 --> 00:18:54,361
Hey, Hammock, what are you doing?

277
00:18:58,320 --> 00:18:59,440
Hey Hancock.

278
00:19:08,120 --> 00:19:10,357
My life is finally complete.

279
00:19:10,440 --> 00:19:11,940
I can die happy.

280
00:19:14,720 --> 00:19:17,037
Hey, you can turn that lady back now!

281
00:19:17,120 --> 00:19:18,591
I should be fine up here.

282
00:19:19,160 --> 00:19:20,117
Say it, Luffy.

283
00:19:20,200 --> 00:19:21,617
Say my name again.

284
00:19:21,700 --> 00:19:23,497
This is taking too long?

285
00:19:23,580 --> 00:19:25,520
This situation is unprecedented.

286
00:19:25,860 --> 00:19:27,919
She's probably just being thorough.

287
00:19:28,420 --> 00:19:30,680
Oh, that's so naughty!

288
00:19:31,840 --> 00:19:34,252
Get your mind out of the gutter, damn it!

289
00:19:36,360 --> 00:19:37,190
Uh,

290
00:19:37,273 --> 00:19:38,103
Vice-Wordant Hannibal,

291
00:19:38,186 --> 00:19:41,377
we're not getting any visuals from the
surveillance down in the examination room.

292
00:19:41,460 --> 00:19:43,657
Is there something going on
in there we don't know about?

293
00:19:43,740 --> 00:19:44,570
Huh?

294
00:19:45,680 --> 00:19:47,621
Domino, something wrong in there?

295
00:19:50,160 --> 00:19:50,990
Huh?

296
00:19:54,280 --> 00:19:56,560
We have completed the body search sir

297
00:19:59,000 --> 00:20:01,457
Scratch that last report
everything is fine here.

298
00:20:01,540 --> 00:20:03,217
I hope I didn't cause a problem sir.

299
00:20:03,300 --> 00:20:04,888
Did the exam take too long?

300
00:20:05,820 --> 00:20:06,650
No

301
00:20:08,180 --> 00:20:09,617
Everything's fine on our end, too.

302
00:20:09,700 --> 00:20:13,157
I See that your guests are treated
as poorly as your prisoners here?

303
00:20:13,240 --> 00:20:15,497
Surely an empress
deserves better than this!

304
00:20:15,580 --> 00:20:20,400
It is a pity but in Impel Down we can't
afford to make exceptions to the rules.

305
00:20:20,960 --> 00:20:24,020
I wonder why I can't shake
this strange feeling.

306
00:20:24,680 --> 00:20:25,597
Lead the way!

307
00:20:25,680 --> 00:20:28,217
Ah, yes, if you'll let
me in front, please!

308
00:20:28,300 --> 00:20:30,340
Or just go that way.

309
00:20:34,360 --> 00:20:35,880
Before we visit Ace,

310
00:20:36,040 --> 00:20:39,037
we'll take this elevator to what
we call the burning heat floor.

311
00:20:39,120 --> 00:20:41,577
Where we'll stop by the
Warden Magellan's office.

312
00:20:41,660 --> 00:20:44,954
Fair warning, as the name
implies, it's quite hot there.

313
00:20:51,480 --> 00:20:54,080
Luffy be bold but be safe.

314
00:20:56,020 --> 00:20:57,057
Bye Hancock!

315
00:20:57,140 --> 00:20:58,060
Thank you.

316
00:20:59,420 --> 00:21:01,280
He really does love me.

317
00:21:03,240 --> 00:21:05,337
He's Empress Hancock. What's wrong?

318
00:21:05,420 --> 00:21:06,537
Do you need mouth to mouth?

319
00:21:06,620 --> 00:21:07,450
Are you ill?

320
00:21:07,533 --> 00:21:10,100
You were fine just a
moment ago. What happened?

321
00:21:17,460 --> 00:21:19,737
Okay, not sure where to
take things from here.

322
00:21:19,820 --> 00:21:22,377
Hancock said Ace is probably underwater.

323
00:21:22,460 --> 00:21:25,377
Looks like that elevator
might head down a long way.

324
00:21:25,460 --> 00:21:29,820
Oh yeah, the fever card
might come in handy.

325
00:21:53,060 --> 00:21:55,178
Looks like they grabbed dinner, too.

326
00:21:55,420 --> 00:21:56,302
Open the hatch!

327
00:22:00,360 --> 00:22:01,280
Nice work.

328
00:22:01,880 --> 00:22:04,174
Get it to the fridge and we'll be done.

329
00:22:07,840 --> 00:22:08,897
We found him!

330
00:22:08,980 --> 00:22:09,810
That's buggy.

331
00:22:09,893 --> 00:22:12,337
The clown prisoner from level
one community cell number

332
00:22:12,420 --> 00:22:15,714
four in the hallway in front
of solitary cell number 22?

333
00:22:18,660 --> 00:22:21,120
Stupid snail, this is all your fault!

334
00:22:28,080 --> 00:22:32,577
You blew it, buggy old don't come crying
to us when they're torturing you to death.

335
00:22:32,660 --> 00:22:33,897
Serves you right, you dummy!

336
00:22:33,980 --> 00:22:36,215
Yeah, he'll wish he was dead for sure.

337
00:22:38,980 --> 00:22:41,160
Oh, here come the Bligotti.

338
00:22:41,400 --> 00:22:42,380
Happy hunting.

339
00:22:42,800 --> 00:22:44,080
Make him suffer.

340
00:22:49,900 --> 00:22:53,120
The fever guard keeps leading
me down, but now what?

341
00:22:53,440 --> 00:22:54,852
Guess I'm out of stairs.

342
00:22:59,540 --> 00:23:00,520
All right, men.

343
00:23:00,680 --> 00:23:02,940
We're looking for prisoner 8200. What?

344
00:23:03,180 --> 00:23:04,460
The stupid clown?

345
00:23:06,340 --> 00:23:08,257
No one knew he had Devil Fruit powers.

346
00:23:08,340 --> 00:23:09,634
You got the handcuffs?

347
00:23:09,760 --> 00:23:10,760
Yeah, we're good.

348
00:23:11,940 --> 00:23:12,820
Let's move.

349
00:23:13,760 --> 00:23:15,320
Split up and flank him.

350
00:23:18,880 --> 00:23:20,920
Cool. I made it. Hurry!

351
00:23:23,020 --> 00:23:24,260
Wonder what's up.

352
00:23:30,260 --> 00:23:32,500
So all of these are prison cells?

353
00:23:35,180 --> 00:23:36,977
What's that? Huh?

354
00:23:37,060 --> 00:23:38,460
I gotta get moving.

355
00:23:40,640 --> 00:23:41,470
Huh?

356
00:23:41,780 --> 00:23:43,900
Hey, hey, hey, hey!

357
00:23:44,580 --> 00:23:45,700
Buddy, slow down.

358
00:23:46,000 --> 00:23:46,937
Hold on a second.

359
00:23:47,020 --> 00:23:47,850
Kind of busy.

360
00:23:47,933 --> 00:23:51,117
Yeah, that's what it looks like, but how
the heck did you get out of your cell?

361
00:23:51,200 --> 00:23:52,480
Hey, what's going on?

362
00:23:52,860 --> 00:23:54,160
I didn't get out.

363
00:23:54,300 --> 00:23:55,888
I came in from the outside.

364
00:23:56,220 --> 00:23:57,797
Well, bye. Hey, hold up.

365
00:23:57,880 --> 00:23:59,900
There's no way that's the truth.

366
00:24:00,220 --> 00:24:01,480
Uh-huh, it's so true.

367
00:24:01,680 --> 00:24:03,137
You don't look like a jailer.

368
00:24:03,220 --> 00:24:05,797
So who are you and why
the hell are you here?

369
00:24:05,880 --> 00:24:08,292
He's not behind bars, so maybe it's true.

370
00:24:08,380 --> 00:24:10,733
You guys have some really bad attitudes.

371
00:24:11,360 --> 00:24:12,190
Wait a sec.

372
00:24:12,273 --> 00:24:13,877
Any of you know where I can find Ace?

373
00:24:13,960 --> 00:24:14,880
Uh, Ace?

374
00:24:15,780 --> 00:24:16,660
Wait, Ace?

375
00:24:16,820 --> 00:24:18,240
You mean, him?

376
00:24:18,720 --> 00:24:20,360
The guy on death row?

377
00:24:21,920 --> 00:24:22,750
That's the one.

378
00:24:22,833 --> 00:24:25,291
I came here to bust him out of this place.

379
00:24:25,720 --> 00:24:27,249
Yeah, good luck with that.

380
00:24:27,380 --> 00:24:31,097
We don't get a lot of info down here,
but I heard they just brought him in.

381
00:24:31,180 --> 00:24:34,137
If that's true and he is here,
then he's got to be on level five.

382
00:24:34,220 --> 00:24:36,017
No way you're getting down there.

383
00:24:36,100 --> 00:24:37,276
You're screwed, pal.

384
00:24:37,460 --> 00:24:39,437
That's the floor where
they hold all the prisoners

385
00:24:39,520 --> 00:24:41,957
with the bounty of a
hundred million or more.

386
00:24:42,040 --> 00:24:43,220
Level five, huh?

387
00:24:43,600 --> 00:24:45,020
Oh, and by the way, pal,

388
00:24:45,240 --> 00:24:49,897
why you here you think you could run to
the jailer's room and pick us up some keys?

389
00:24:49,980 --> 00:24:50,810
Yeah, buddy.

390
00:24:50,893 --> 00:24:52,057
Wouldn't be no trouble, right?

391
00:24:52,140 --> 00:24:53,857
This has got to be destiny, man.

392
00:24:53,940 --> 00:24:56,137
I mean, what else would
bring us together like this?

393
00:24:56,220 --> 00:24:58,926
It's like you were born
to set us free, right?

394
00:25:01,880 --> 00:25:03,174
What are those things?

395
00:25:04,780 --> 00:25:06,080
Stop the body!

396
00:25:06,240 --> 00:25:08,840
I don't like him! Run! Hurry!

397
00:25:09,040 --> 00:25:10,393
They're gonna kill you!

398
00:25:19,780 --> 00:25:21,177
I take him back!

399
00:25:21,260 --> 00:25:22,160
I like you!

400
00:25:22,480 --> 00:25:23,680
Right side!

401
00:25:24,420 --> 00:25:26,020
And left side!

402
00:25:28,080 --> 00:25:29,220
You're tight!

403
00:25:30,420 --> 00:25:32,297
How you like that, suckers?

404
00:25:32,380 --> 00:25:33,757
You can cut me all you want!

405
00:25:33,840 --> 00:25:35,428
I ate the chop-chop fruits!

406
00:25:40,680 --> 00:25:41,560
Straw rats!

407
00:25:42,200 --> 00:25:44,220
What the hell are you doing here?

408
00:25:47,620 --> 00:25:48,500
Oh, buggy.

409
00:25:49,500 --> 00:25:51,794
Thanks for reminding me why I hate you!

410
00:25:52,120 --> 00:25:54,737
I see prison hasn't made
you any less annoying.

411
00:25:54,820 --> 00:25:57,997
Speaking of, guess that King of the
Pirates thing ain't working out too well.

412
00:25:58,080 --> 00:25:59,237
I came here on my own.

413
00:25:59,320 --> 00:26:01,737
Only dumb people like you get
caught and thrown in jail.

414
00:26:01,820 --> 00:26:02,650
Say what?

415
00:26:02,733 --> 00:26:06,337
You threw yourself in jail and
you're calling me the dumb one?

416
00:26:06,420 --> 00:26:08,244
You must have known I was here.

417
00:26:08,480 --> 00:26:09,317
That's the real reason.

418
00:26:09,400 --> 00:26:10,477
You're broken, isn't it?

419
00:26:10,560 --> 00:26:12,780
To save me.

420
00:26:14,680 --> 00:26:16,420
I'm not into you, weirdo.

421
00:26:16,560 --> 00:26:19,148
Just shut up and get
the hell out of my way.

422
00:26:19,340 --> 00:26:21,897
I told Hancock I'd take
care of myself and you

423
00:26:21,980 --> 00:26:24,897
got all these stupid axe
monkeys chasing after me.

424
00:26:24,980 --> 00:26:26,220
Oh, I see.

425
00:26:26,360 --> 00:26:28,066
This is all about you, is it?

426
00:26:35,640 --> 00:26:37,600
This is supposed to be a cinch.

427
00:26:37,800 --> 00:26:40,137
I called it Buggy's Peaceful Escape Plan.

428
00:26:40,220 --> 00:26:42,017
Does this look peaceful to you?

429
00:26:42,100 --> 00:26:43,120
Who cares?

430
00:26:46,200 --> 00:26:48,082
They're surrounding us, damn it.

431
00:26:48,200 --> 00:26:49,840
I hate this.

432
00:26:50,220 --> 00:26:52,477
Hey, should we just beat those things up?

433
00:26:52,560 --> 00:26:55,037
Easy for you to say you
haven't been tortured.

434
00:26:55,120 --> 00:26:58,757
Oh, how my delicate body has suffered
from the blows of these monsters.

435
00:26:58,840 --> 00:27:01,457
Why can't they think I'm
running away in the first place?

436
00:27:01,540 --> 00:27:04,240
Yeah, but I wasn't
planning to lose. Right.

437
00:27:04,480 --> 00:27:05,917
Clearly you've thought this out.

438
00:27:06,000 --> 00:27:07,294
I'm on a mission here.

439
00:27:07,440 --> 00:27:11,381
My cover's already been blown, so
I gotta get this done in a hurry.

440
00:27:12,780 --> 00:27:17,217
You know, that's the number one reason
why I hate you and that redhead so much.

441
00:27:17,300 --> 00:27:21,006
Both of you are always so optimistic
in the worst way possible.

442
00:27:24,660 --> 00:27:25,580
Alright, fine.

443
00:27:25,780 --> 00:27:27,777
I'll go along with your crazy plan.

444
00:27:27,860 --> 00:27:29,640
It's not like I have a choice!

445
00:27:31,100 --> 00:27:32,037
Shhh!

446
00:27:32,120 --> 00:27:33,500
Time for my specialty!

447
00:27:35,760 --> 00:27:37,300
Causing chaos!

448
00:27:38,140 --> 00:27:39,400
Works for me!
